---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const CHECKED_ON = '22 August 2026';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'My accountant asked for Sage. What do I tell them?',
    a: 'That you are running the shop on QuadERP and will export whatever they need. Their work happens in their tool, yours happens at the counter, and the export is the handover between the two.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does QuadERP produce accounts my accountant can use?',
    a: 'It produces a profit and loss and an aged receivables list, plus a full export of the underlying records. It does not produce a trial balance or a balance sheet, so those get built from the export.',
  },
  {
    /* Replaces "Is training included?", whose answer described the optional
       guided setup (us loading products and training staff). That offer went
       on 8 October 2026 and the site does not describe what the one-time
       setup fee covers, so the question it answered honestly is this one. */
    q: 'Can my staff try it before we pay?',
    a: 'Yes. The live demo is a fully stocked demo store that needs no account, so whoever stands behind the counter, which is normally not the owner, can practise on it first. There is no free trial: the setup fee and first year are paid before you start, so the demo is the place to find out.',
  },
];
---

<PageLayout page="sage-alternative-ghana" faqs={faqs} faqHeading="Questions people ask when comparing">
    <p>
        Sage is built for people whose job is accounts. That is a real audience and it is well
        served. The awkward part is that in a small retail business, the person who has to use the
        system every day is a cashier, and the person who wants to look at it in the evening is
        the owner. Neither of them is an accountant.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is actually going to use it</h2>
    <p>
        This is the question that decides the purchase, and it is usually asked last. A system
        designed around a chart of accounts assumes a user who thinks in a chart of accounts.
        Hand that to someone serving customers at a counter and one of two things happens: they
        do not use it, or somebody re-enters the day's takings afterwards.
    </p>
    <p>
        QuadERP is designed around the counter first. Ringing up a sale is the primary action, and
        the money follows from it rather than being typed in separately.
    </p>

    <div class="erp-compare-wrap">
        <table class="erp-compare-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Designed around</th><th>QuadERP</th><th>An accounts package</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>The primary user</td><td>Whoever is at the counter</td><td>Whoever keeps the books</td></tr>
                <tr><td>The first action of the day</td><td>Sell something</td><td>Record a transaction</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Stock on the shelf</td><td>Central</td><td>Varies, often an add-on</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Several branches</td><td>Yes, GHS 200 a year each after the first</td><td>Varies by tier</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Double entry and statutory reporting</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>What the price depends on</td><td>Branches, never features</td><td>Varies by tier</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p class="erp-checked-on">
        The QuadERP column is checked against what ships today. The right-hand column describes
        accounts packages as a category, not one vendor's current tier list. Checked {CHECKED_ON}.
    </p>

    <h2>We are not asking you to sack your accountant</h2>
    <p>
        Keep them. What changes is what you hand over: real records with dates, staff names and
        receipts attached, instead of a bag and a best guess. That normally makes their job
        smaller. What QuadERP does not do on the accounts side is written out plainly on
        <a href="/accounting-software-ghana/">the accounting page</a>, including no VAT return and
        no filing.
    </p>

    <h2>What you get instead</h2>
    <p>
        A till that runs on a phone, stock that moves when you sell, alerts before you run out,
        a record of which staff member did what, and a number for takings you can look at from
        home. Priced in cedis, with every feature in one yearly price, and a live demo you can try
        before you pay anything.
    </p>
</PageLayout>
